   "source": {
    "label": "thm:OCO-main-result",
    "number": "Theorem (thm:OCO-main-result)",
    "quote": "Suppose $C \\ge \\ln T + 1$, and consider $\\cW(\\gA, \\gD)$, where $\\gA$ is DW-FTRL. With rates $\\eta_t = \\tfrac{D/G}{\\sqrt{\\dtot + T}}$ and $\\gD$ from Corollary~\\ref{cor:pareto-scheduler}, $\\cW(\\gA, \\gD)$ guarantees $\\widebar R_T(x^*) = O(GD\\sqrt{\\dtot + T})$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Proof gives explicit 18GD sqrt(d_tot+T) + GD. Expectation over the scheduler randomness; losses oblivious. Also extends to non-preemptive variant (appendix)."
  },
